# switchboard client registry — copy to clients.conf (gitignored). One row per client.
# Fields (pipe-delimited):  slug | account | git_name | git_email | ssh_key | workspace
#
#   slug       short name you'll type:  `./work acme`
#   account    a label for YOU: which Claude login this client uses (e.g. own | client)
#   git_name   name commits should use for this client
#   git_email  email commits should use for this client
#   ssh_key    path to the SSH key for this client's git remote (or - for your default)
#   workspace  where this client's repos live (or - to default to <repo>/<slug>)
#
# Each client automatically gets its OWN isolated CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR at <repo>/config/<slug>:
# separate Claude login, MCP servers, and credentials, so clients never mix.

acme   | own    | Alex Example | alex@acme.example   | ~/.ssh/id_acme   | ~/Work/acme
globex | client | Alex Example | alex@globex.example | -                | -
